{
  "v": 11,
  "label": "a copy taking the body the member under the bare Message-ID of the target holds releases that body from it, for the next upgrade to fetch",
  "note": "INBOX holds basic-1@example.org with its body. Archive holds a member stating the same Message-ID under the bare key, holding the same body: listed before Archive held any other member stating it, it agreed with INBOX's row on subject, date, sender and size and linked that body, though it may be another message, as neverest's live test of 2026-11-24 found on Stalwart (a move into a mailbox holding another message stating the moved one's Message-ID, of one size, left the target's own member holding the moved body). The copy into Archive is keyed by the identity minted over the provisional handle it derives and holds INBOX's body. Archive now holds two members stating one Message-ID, sharing one body no fetch confirmed and no server object id names as one content, so the write releases it from the bare one as a release does: back to Meta, its summary, flags, binding and seq kept, its base naming no body. The next Full upgrade fetches it, never linking it by agreement beside the copy (vector 222). Left as it was, the bare member would hold the copied body for ever, a message's body never fetched again (SYNC.md §6, §7; STORAGE §9, §11.4, §14)",
